.el .ds Aq '
.TH swarm-mr-comment 1  "swarm 0.2.1" "Swarmgit manual"
.SH NAME
swarm\-mr\-comment \- Comment on a merge request, a file in it, or another comment
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBswarm mr comment\fR [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-message\fR] [\fB\-R\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-\-line\fR] [\fB\-\-reply\-to\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIMR\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Comment on a merge request, a file in it, or another comment
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
The comment; without it your git editor opens
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
A repo ID or link; by default the swarm remote of this clone
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
File the comment is about
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Use what is already here instead of syncing first
.TP
\fB\-\-line\fR \fI<LINE>\fR
Line of that file
.TP
\fB\-\-reply\-to\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR
Comment being answered, by the ID shown before it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIMR\fR]
Its branch or ID (default: the current branch)
